  "rules_and_architecture": [
    "Grant an exact graveyard incarnation Harmonize through cleanup; permission survives departure of the granting permanent and is distinct from intrinsic Harmonize.",
    "Parse immutable printed mana notation using the existing shared printed_cost parser/options. The selected definition supplies actual colors, hybrid/twobrid alternatives and X count; mana value never substitutes for mana cost.",
    "Intrinsic Harmonize separately declares its alternate-cost X symbol count. Generic payment X and printed mana-value X are independent inputs; ordinary X interval search stays bounded by threshold segments and binary search.",
    "Harmonize keeps its existing optional creature declaration, locked power discount, ordered tap clause and exact source exile replacement on every stack departure.",
    "Delve is a generic-only mana payment after total cost locking, shared with existing Convoke/Improvise/Waterbend contributor state and all existing mana/additional cost participants. It does not generate mana or reduce the total cost.",
    "Exact selected grave cards remain reserved until the mana payment commits, then ordinary simultaneous zone movement commits their exile. Borrowed cost worlds project those departures for later obligations.",
    "Availability uses the live provider, player and selected spell definition. A source may depart after Delve payment as a later cost; losing the only grant during mana production cannot fund Delve afterward.",
    "Before funding a proposal, the borrowed world projects the known exact spell source out of its origin to Stack, with casting controller and graveyard-left fact. The real Game is never mutated by that preview; the proposed spell cannot fuel its own or a mana child additional cost."
  ],
  "focused_tests": [
    "granted_harmonize_uses_printed_colored_cost_exact_card_and_independent_duration",
    "harmonize_grant_expires_and_does_not_follow_a_new_graveyard_incarnation",
    "granted_and_intrinsic_harmonize_costs_remain_separate_and_countered_spell_is_exiled",
    "granted_harmonize_preserves_hybrid_and_twobrid_symbols",
    "x_in_printed_or_harmonize_cost_is_chosen_paid_and_does_not_change_printed_value_rules",
    "delve_pays_only_generic_and_commits_exact_graveyard_cards",
    "delve_respects_locked_taxes_reductions_and_harmonize_stack_origin",
    "sacrificed_mana_producer_can_be_delved_but_a_departed_grant_cannot_supply_delve",
    "additional_graveyard_cost_and_delve_reserve_distinct_cards_in_either_order",
    "delve_selection_is_owned_raw_index_restorable_and_private",
    "delve_provider_can_leave_in_a_later_cost_after_mana_is_paid",
    "delve_uses_the_same_total_from_hand_exile_and_permitted_library_top",
    "mana_child_must_preserve_its_ancestors_distinct_delve_resources",
    "granted_harmonize_recomputes_the_cost_of_an_existing_selected_spell_face",
    "harmonize_exiles_on_a_stack_departure_that_would_return_the_spell_to_hand",
    "delve_shares_one_locked_payment_with_convoke_and_improvise",
    "delve_cannot_pay_a_required_colorless_symbol",
    "delve_obeys_a_live_graveyard_exile_prohibition",
    "a_proposed_graveyard_spell_cannot_pay_a_mana_childs_graveyard_cost"
  ],
  "meaningful_contracts": [
    "Both seats: exact printed U cannot be paid by generic mana or grave exiles; one ungranted identical card stays uncastable.",
    "Actual ETB grant resolution; source removal, cleanup expiry and graveyard leave/reentry invalidation.",
    "Separate intrinsic/granted routes, colored hybrid and twobrid payments; normal and alternate X declarations, over-domain transactional rejection and printed stack mana value.",
    "Resolved, countered and returned-to-hand Harmonize spells all exile; selected Omen cost uses its inset symbols and Harmonize overrides Omen library shuffle.",
    "Hand, exact granted graveyard, permitted exile and library-top origins; locked taxes and reductions compose with Delve.",
    "Own exact physical graveyard cards only; duplicate, opponent, source and excessive contributions rejected; required C always uses real mana; live exile prohibition respected.",
    "Convoke and Improvise each share the mana frame with Delve. Later additional costs reserve distinct grave cards, and a provider may be sacrificed only after paying the Delve-enabled mana clause.",
    "A sacrificed mana producer becomes grave fuel; sacrificing the sole Delve provider before payment removes Delve.",
    "A costed mana child is rejected when it strands its parent, and succeeds with one distinct additional grave card. Precast negative/positive witnesses prove a proposed graveyard spell cannot pay its own mana child, with and without Delve.",
    "Owned raw/index children, sibling divergence, parent disposal, both observations/privacy, stale revision restore and illegal-action snapshot/revision preservation."
  ],
